course: dictionary
lesson: 6151
title: Millionaire in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A millionaire is a person whose money and property are worth at least a million pounds, dollars or other units of money. Property means things you own, such as a house or land.
explain: «Chloe said her dad was a millionaire» is a big claim. When Mia visited a normal flat with a cosy sofa, Chloe went red, so the clues suggest the story was not true.
explain: Sometimes a word is used to describe a feeling. «Leo got three gift cards for his birthday and felt like a millionaire» does not mean Leo had a million pounds. It means he felt very rich and happy.
explain: Mia's «lush» is Welsh and West Country slang for lovely. Context tells you the meaning: she is praising the flat and the sofa. A dictionary can confirm it.
fact: A millionaire is a person with money and property worth at least a million.
fact: «Million» means 1,000,000, which is a thousand thousands.
fact: «Become a millionaire» means to reach a fortune of a million or more.
fact: A «self-made millionaire» got rich through their own work and effort.
fact: People say they «feel like a millionaire» when they are very happy, even if they are not one.
exercise: «Chloe said her dad was a millionaire.» What is a millionaire? | A person who lives in a very big flat | *A person with money and property worth at least a million | A person who can count to a million | A person who always wins games
exercise: «Leo got three gift cards for his birthday and felt like a millionaire.» What does this suggest? | He really had a million pounds in the bank | He wanted to count to a million | He was ill in bed | *He felt very rich and happy
exercise: In maths, how many is one million? | 1,000 | 10,000 | *1,000,000 | 100,000
test:
Which word in «Your flat's lush, I love your sofa» means lovely, in Welsh and West Country slang? | flat | *lush | sofa | love
What does «self-made millionaire» suggest? | *Someone who got rich through their own work | Someone who inherited a fortune from their family | Someone who was born in a big house | Someone who won a school prize
exam: What does «become a millionaire» mean? | To buy a very big house | To lose all your money | To count up to one million | *To reach money and property worth at least a million
